# Tests — MSA Schedule 4 chronic failure

Assertion-based tests for `Chronic_failure`. L-6.1's two triggers are
independent, so they are tested independently as well as together:

  * three consecutive failing periods, and the two-in-a-row case that is one
    short of it, and the case where a single good month breaks the run;
  * four failing periods inside a rolling twelve-month window, with a pattern
    that satisfies this trigger while never producing three in a row, and the
    same four failures spread just too wide to fit any twelve-month window;
  * the rolling window itself at exactly twelve months and at thirteen.

"Less than 99.90%" is tested at exactly 99.90% (not a failure, and it breaks a
run) and at 99.89%. L-6.2's 30-day exercise window is tested at day 30 and day
31, both where notice has been given and where it has not, and the case where
no right ever arose is tested with a far-future assessment date: a right that
does not exist cannot lapse.

> Using ChronicFailure

## Helper

A Measurement Period is a calendar month, identified by its first and last
day. This constructor keeps the histories below readable; it encodes nothing.

```catala
declaration mp
  content ChronicFailure.PeriodAvailability
  depends on
    starts content date,
    ends content date,
    pct content decimal
  equals
    ChronicFailure.PeriodAvailability {
      -- period_start: starts
      -- period_end: ends
      -- availability_percentage: pct
    }
```

## L6_1_ThreeConsecutive

L-6.1 first trigger: three consecutive Measurement Periods below 99.90%. The
right arises, the completing period is the third of the three, and the second
trigger is not satisfied because there are only three failures in all.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ThreeConsecutive:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ThreeConsecutive:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = true
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-03-31|
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-04-30|
  assertion r.notice_period_days = 30
  assertion r.early_termination_charges_payable = false
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly

L-6.1: two consecutive failures are not three. Neither trigger is satisfied,
so no right arises and there is no deadline to compute.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_TwoConsecutiveOnly:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.95
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Absent
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

## L6_1_GapResetsTheRun

L-6.1: "each of three consecutive Measurement Periods". One good month between
failures breaks the run, and three failures are not four, so neither trigger
fires.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_GapResetsTheRun:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_GapResetsTheRun:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.95;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-05-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
```

## L6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure

L-6.1 requires the Availability Percentage to be "less than 99.90%", which is
strict and matches L-3.1. Three months at exactly 99.90% are three months in
which the Service Level was met.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineIsNotAFailure:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.90;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.90;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.90
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 0
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
```

## L6_1_JustBelowIsAFailure

L-6.1: one hundredth of a percentage point lower and the same three months
trigger the right.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_JustBelowIsAFailure:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_JustBelowIsAFailure:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.89;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.89;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.89
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = true
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-03-31|
```

## L6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineBreaksARun

L-6.1: a month at exactly 99.90% sits in the middle of four bad months and
defeats the consecutive trigger, because the run must be of three periods each
below 99.90%. The second trigger needs four failures and there are only three.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineBreaksARun:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ExactlyNinetyNinePointNineBreaksARun:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 98.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.90;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 98.00;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 98.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-05-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
```

## L6_1_FourInTwelveMonthsWithoutThreeConsecutive

L-6.1 second trigger, standing alone. Four failing Measurement Periods inside
twelve months, alternating with good ones, so the first trigger is never
satisfied. The completing period is July, the fourth failure.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_FourInTwelveMonthsWithoutThreeConsecutive:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_FourInTwelveMonthsWithoutThreeConsecutive:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.50;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.95;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.10;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-05-01|, |2025-05-31|, 98.00;
           mp of |2025-06-01|, |2025-06-30|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-07-01|, |2025-07-31|, 97.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-08-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-08-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 4
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = true
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion (number of r.completing_periods) = 1
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-07-31|
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-08-30|
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_1_ThreeInTwelveMonthsIsNotEnough

L-6.1 second trigger needs four. Three scattered failures satisfy neither
trigger.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_ThreeInTwelveMonthsIsNotEnough:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_ThreeInTwelveMonthsIsNotEnough:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.50;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.95;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.10;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-05-01|, |2025-05-31|, 98.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-06-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-06-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 3
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
```

## L6_1_RollingWindowExactlyTwelveMonths

L-6.1: January and December of the same year are inside one rolling
twelve-month period, so four failures spanning exactly twelve months trigger
the right.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_RollingWindowExactlyTwelveMonths:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_RollingWindowExactlyTwelveMonths:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-05-01|, |2025-05-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-09-01|, |2025-09-30|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-12-01|, |2025-12-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2026-01-15|
    }
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = true
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-12-31|
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2026-01-30|
```

## L6_1_RollingWindowJustTooWide

L-6.1: move the earliest failure back one month and the four no longer fit any
twelve-month period. No right arises.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_RollingWindowJustTooWide:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_RollingWindowJustTooWide:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2024-12-01|, |2024-12-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-05-01|, |2025-05-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-09-01|, |2025-09-30|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-12-01|, |2025-12-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2026-01-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2026-01-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 4
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
```

## L6_1_FourSpreadBeyondTwelveMonths

L-6.1: four failures spread over two years, no two adjacent and never four
within twelve months.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_FourSpreadBeyondTwelveMonths:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_FourSpreadBeyondTwelveMonths:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2024-01-01|, |2024-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2024-08-01|, |2024-08-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-10-01|, |2025-10-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-11-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-11-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 4
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = false
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = false
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
```

## L6_1_BothTriggersAndTwoOccurrences

L-6.1: a history can complete the pattern more than once, and both triggers
can be satisfied. Six failures in two runs of three: March completes the first
consecutive run, September the second, and July, August and September each
complete a rolling four. L-6.2 assesses the earliest occurrence, March.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_BothTriggersAndTwoOccurrences:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_BothTriggersAndTwoOccurrences:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-04-01|, |2025-04-30|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-05-01|, |2025-05-31|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-06-01|, |2025-06-30|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-07-01|, |2025-07-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-08-01|, |2025-08-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-09-01|, |2025-09-30|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-20|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-20|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 6
  assertion r.consecutive_trigger = true
  assertion r.rolling_trigger = true
  assertion r.right_arisen = true
  assertion (number of r.completing_periods) = 4
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Present content |2025-03-31|
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-04-30|
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_2_NoticeOnDayThirty

L-6.2: "within 30 days after the end of the Measurement Period which gives
rise to it" is inclusive of the thirtieth day. Notice on 30 April, from a
March trigger, is in time.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_NoticeOnDayThirty:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_NoticeOnDayThirty:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-15|
      -- notice_given: true
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-30|
    }
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-04-30|
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_2_NoticeOnDayThirtyOne

L-6.2: one day later and the right lapses in respect of that occurrence.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_NoticeOnDayThirtyOne:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_NoticeOnDayThirtyOne:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-15|
      -- notice_given: true
      -- notice_date: |2025-05-01|
    }
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Present content |2025-04-30|
  assertion r.right_lapsed = true
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

## L6_2_StillOpenOnDayThirty

L-6.2: with no notice yet given, the right is still exercisable up to and
including the thirtieth day.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_StillOpenOnDayThirty:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_StillOpenOnDayThirty:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-30|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-30|
    }
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = true
```

## L6_2_LapsedUnexercised

L-6.2: the window closes on the thirty-first day and the right lapses even
though nothing has been done with it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_LapsedUnexercised:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_LapsedUnexercised:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.00;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.00
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2025-05-01|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-05-01|
    }
  assertion r.right_lapsed = true
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

## L6_2_NoRightCannotLapse

L-6.2 lapses "the right in L-6.1". Where no right ever arose there is nothing
to lapse, however long ago the history ended — the lapse rule repeats
`right_arisen` from its parent rather than inheriting it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_2_NoRightCannotLapse:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_2_NoRightCannotLapse:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: [
           mp of |2025-01-01|, |2025-01-31|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-02-01|, |2025-02-28|, 99.99;
           mp of |2025-03-01|, |2025-03-31|, 99.99
         ]
      -- assessment_date: |2030-01-01|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2030-01-01|
    }
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
  assertion r.exercise_deadline = Absent
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```

## L6_1_EmptyHistory

L-6.1 over no history at all: no failing periods, no trigger, no right.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestL6_1_EmptyHistory:
  output r content ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight

scope TestL6_1_EmptyHistory:
  definition r equals
    output of ChronicFailure.ChronicFailureRight with {
      -- availability_history: []
      -- assessment_date: |2025-04-15|
      -- notice_given: false
      -- notice_date: |2025-04-15|
    }
  assertion (number of r.failing_periods) = 0
  assertion r.right_arisen = false
  assertion r.trigger_period_end = Absent
  assertion r.right_lapsed = false
  assertion r.right_exercisable = false
```
